### Key Results

| Analysis | Coefficient | SE | Conclusion |
|----------|-------------|-----|------------|
| **Replication** (1996-2018) |
| Dem Vote Share (quad) | 0.007 | 0.007 | Null - matches original |
| Turnout (quad) | 0.022 | 0.007 | +2.2pp - matches original |
| **Extension** (1996-2024) |
| Dem Vote Share (quad) | 0.005 | 0.004 | Null persists |
| VBM × Post2018 | -0.005 | 0.008 | No differential effect |
| CA VCA Effect (quad) | 0.006 | 0.004 | No partisan impact |

### Conclusion

**Universal vote-by-mail has no partisan impact on elections.** This finding from Thompson et al. (2020) is:
1. Successfully replicated with coefficients within 0.002 of published values
2. Extended through 2024 with consistent null results
3. Robust to COVID-era changes, California VCA expansion, and various specification checks

The complete academic paper, code, data, and documentation are ready for review.

